## 🔹 Historical Examples

### 🐛 Morris Worm (1988)

* One of the first major internet worms
* Exploited buffer overflow in Unix services
* Infected ~10% of the internet at the time

### ❤️ Heartbleed Bug (2014)

* A vulnerability in OpenSSL
* Allowed attackers to read sensitive memory from servers
* Exposed passwords, keys, and private data

These incidents show how dangerous memory-related vulnerabilities can be.

